---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import aboutPhoto from "@/assets/about.png";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description:
		"About ChihYing Yen — data and machine learning engineer, Rust ML author, lifelong learner.",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-8">About Me</h1>
	<Image
		alt="ChihYing Yen"
		class="border-special-light mb-8 h-40 w-40 rounded-full border object-cover object-[center_25%]"
		densities={[1.5, 2]}
		src={aboutPhoto}
		width={160}
	/>
	<div
		class="mb-8 inline-flex gap-1 rounded-full border border-special-light p-1 text-xs"
		id="about-lang"
		role="group"
		aria-label="Language"
	>
		<button
			class="rounded-full px-3 py-1 font-semibold transition-colors"
			data-lang-btn="en"
			type="button"
		>
			English
		</button>
		<button
			class="rounded-full px-3 py-1 font-semibold transition-colors"
			data-lang-btn="zh"
			type="button"
		>
			中文
		</button>
	</div>

	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none" data-lang="en">
		<p>
			I’m a data and machine learning engineer. I believe that crafting a great
			data solution is much like forging a fine tool: choosing the right
			material, controlling the heat, and hammering it again and again until
			something genuinely useful is tempered into shape. <em>Xavier’s Data
			Forge</em> embodies this philosophy, treating raw, messy data as iron ore
			waiting to be smelted, and refining it with a craftsman’s discipline into
			reliable insights and systems.
		</p>
		<p>
			With over five years of hands-on experience across the materials and
			telecom industries, I’ve built machine learning solutions ranging from
			discovering new materials with Bayesian Optimization to catching
			production-line defects with YOLO before they turn into real problems. My
			MLOps practice and data pipelines are built for stability and
			reproducibility, making sure that what reaches stakeholders is always
			something that holds up to scrutiny.
		</p>
		<p>
			More recently I’ve extended my focus into the Rust ML ecosystem. I’m the
			author of <em>From Pythonista to Rustacean: A Data Practitioner’s First
			Guide to Rust</em> (《從 Pythonista 到 Rustacean：資料從業者的第一本 Rust
			指南》), which walks Python-rooted data professionals into the Rust world,
			covering Rust fundamentals, PyO3 integration, and hands-on AI model
			training with Candle and Burn.
		</p>
		<p>
			I’m also an active open-source contributor. Most recently I’ve worked on
			<em>zerostack</em>, a lightweight, memory-efficient coding agent harness
			written in Rust. From writing technical series to collaborating in the
			open, I’m driven by a lifelong appetite for learning, always hungry for
			new tools and ideas, and always looking for a sharper way to solve the
			problem on the anvil.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none" data-lang="zh" hidden>
		<p>
			我是一名資料／機器學習工程師。我相信打造一個優秀的資料解決方案就像鍛造一件器物，選對素材、掌握火候、反覆敲打，最終才能淬鍊出真正堪用的成品。<em>Xavier’s
			Data Forge（鍛造資料）</em>正是這個理念的體現，把原始、雜亂的資料當作待煉的鐵料，以匠人之心反覆錘鍊成可靠的洞察與系統。
		</p>
		<p>
			我在材料與電信領域累積了超過五年的實戰經驗，從以貝氏最佳化（Bayesian
			Optimization）探索新材料，到運用 YOLO
			在產線缺陷釀成問題之前即時揪出異常，都是我親手打造的機器學習解決方案。我的 MLOps
			與資料管線講求穩定與可重現，確保每一次交付到利害關係人手中的，都是經得起檢驗的成果。
		</p>
		<p>
			近年我將重心延伸至 Rust ML 生態系，著有《從 Pythonista 到 Rustacean：資料從業者的第一本
			Rust 指南》，帶領 Python 出身的資料工作者跨入 Rust 的世界，內容涵蓋 Rust 基礎、PyO3
			整合，以及 Candle／Burn 的 AI 模型訓練實戰。
		</p>
		<p>
			我也持續投入開源貢獻，最近參與了 <em>zerostack</em>，一個以 Rust
			寫成、主打極低記憶體佔用的輕量級 coding agent
			harness。從鐵人賽系列文到開源協作，我始終抱持著終身學習的熱忱，永遠對新的工具與想法保持飢渴，並樂於為每一道難題找到更鋒利的解法。
		</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>

<script>
	function initAboutLang() {
		const group = document.getElementById("about-lang");
		if (!group) return;
		const buttons = group.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-lang-btn]");
		const panels = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-lang]");

		function apply(lang: string) {
			for (const panel of panels) panel.hidden = panel.dataset.lang !== lang;
			for (const btn of buttons) {
				const active = btn.dataset.langBtn === lang;
				btn.classList.toggle("bg-accent", active);
				btn.classList.toggle("text-global-bg", active);
				btn.classList.toggle("text-muted", !active);
				btn.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(active));
			}
			try {
				localStorage.setItem("about-lang", lang);
			} catch {
				/* ignore storage failures (private mode) */
			}
		}

		for (const btn of buttons) {
			btn.addEventListener("click", () => apply(btn.dataset.langBtn || "en"));
		}

		let saved = "en";
		try {
			saved = localStorage.getItem("about-lang") || "en";
		} catch {
			/* ignore */
		}
		apply(saved === "zh" ? "zh" : "en");
	}

	initAboutLang();
	document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", initAboutLang);
</script>
